    "did_you_know": "In 17th-century Holland, scenes of men and women playing music together often had amorous connotations.",
    "early_education_description": null,
    "artlens_description": null,
    "description": "The Utrecht artist Gerrit van Honthorst was internationally known as a portrait painter, but he also gained a reputation as a painter of raucous musical scenes and parties. This drawing was once part of an album of compositional types that the artist showed to prospective patrons. Though the cheerful theme of a man and a woman sharing a song seems innocent, such unions often had amorous or lascivious connotations in 17th-century Holland.",
